{
  "Appointments that repeat by an RFC 5545 rule, with times left out and occurrences changed apart; a question on what a change reaches; an editor of the rule; and the days on the clock of any time zone, summer time included.": "",
  "Recurring appointments": "",
  "An appointment with a `recurrenceRule` is a series: the scheduler shows its occurrences in the days on screen only. `recurrenceException` leaves times out; an appointment whose `recurrenceId` names a series stands in for one of its occurrences. Supported: `FREQ` daily to yearly, `INTERVAL`, `COUNT`, `UNTIL`, `BYDAY` (`2MO`, `-1FR`), `BYMONTHDAY`, `BYMONTH`, `BYYEARDAY`, `BYWEEKNO`, `BYSETPOS`, `WKST`, `BYHOUR`, `BYMINUTE`.": "",
  "Changing a series": "",
  "Moving, resizing, the form and Delete ask the same question. **This one**: a new appointment takes its place (naming its series) and its time is left out of the series. **This and following**: the series ends before it (`UNTIL`, or a smaller `COUNT`) and a new series goes on from it. **The whole series**: every occurrence moves as this one did; a weekly series moved to another day moves its weekdays.": "",
  "With a data source every write goes through its adapter, one after another: the new rows first, then the changes, then the deletes. When a later write fails, the earlier ones are taken back through the adapter; `onDataError` tells what was saved (`saved`, `unsaved`) and whether it was all taken back (`undone`). An occurrence changed apart is an ordinary row, linked to its series by `recurrenceId`; deleting the series asks the adapter for those rows, loaded or not. This example runs from a data source.": "",
  "The recurrence editor": "",
  "The appointment form holds it (`editing.allowRecurrence`). On its own it is `RecurrenceEditor`: the repeat list, every how many, the weekdays, a day of the month or a weekday by its place, the month, the end; a rule it cannot show whole stays as it is until a choice is changed.": "",
  "Time zones": "",
  "`timeZone` puts the days and hours on a zone's clock. A series repeats on the clock of its start's zone (`startDateTimeZone`), so 09:00 in New York stays 09:00 there over summer time. On the night the clocks go forward the skipped hour is passed (a time in it moves on by the hour); on the night they go back a box is as long as the appointment lasts.": "",
  "With `editing.allowTimeZones` the form has one time zone picker and a box, **Separate end time zone**: checked, a second picker sets the end's zone (an appointment whose end zone differs opens with it checked); unchecked, the end follows the start's zone again.": "",
  "Choose this one, this and the following, the whole series.": "",
  "Answer / cancel: the change is dropped and the appointment goes back.": "",
  "An occurrence is named with how its series repeats; one changed apart says so. The marks are only drawn (`aria-hidden`).": "",
  "A modal form: its choices are radio buttons under the question, the first one chosen.": "",
  "A group named \"Repeat\"; the weekdays are toggle buttons (`aria-pressed`) in a group named by its caption; the line in words is polite live text.": "",
  "Units: the marks (`bar`, `chip`, `open`, `past`, `disabled`); a language that has none leaves them out.": "",
  "Unit: the tooltip’s line on how it repeats (`exception`).": "",
  "The editor, its weekday buttons and its line in words.": "",
  "Units of the editor; `day-button` is the weekday buttons’ place; `row-gap`, `column-gap`.": "",
  "`null`: the browser's": "",
  "The clock the days and hours are on, an IANA name (`Europe/Istanbul`). Converted with `Intl` only.": "",
  "What changing or deleting an occurrence reaches. `ask` asks the user; programmatically it is the occurrence unless the call says.": "",
  "The marks of an occurrence and of one changed apart, where the design language draws them.": "",
  "The form holds the recurrence editor.": "",
  "The form holds a time zone picker, and a box \"Separate end time zone\" (`separateEndZone` in the form’s data and `items`) that shows a picker for the end; unchecked, the end follows the start’s zone. Not on all-day appointments.": "",
  "How it repeats: an RFC 5545 rule (`FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,WE`); empty for once.": "",
  "The times left out (`EXDATE`): a text apart by commas (`20261104T090000Z,…`) or a list of dates.": "",
  "On an occurrence changed apart: the key of its series.": "",
  "The zone the start (and the series) and the end are set in; empty for the scheduler’s (the start) and for the start’s (the end).": "",
  "For an occurrence, `scope` says what the change reaches: `occurrence`, `following` or `series`.": "",
  "The same for a delete.": "",
  "Asks the user what a change (`update`) or a delete (`delete`) reaches; resolves to the answer or `null`.": "",
  "The series of an occurrence or of one changed apart; a series itself; else `null`.": "",
  "An occurrence the scheduler made from a rule; one changed apart from its series.": "",
  "The occurrences of a series in a time.": "",
  "How it repeats, in plain words of the locale.": "",
  "`{ appointment, series, action, scopes, scope, cancel }`: set `scope` to answer without the question, narrow `scopes`, or cancel the change.": "",
  "`{ appointment, series, action, scope, byUser }`: `scope` is `null` when the question was cancelled.": "",
  "Now also `scope` and `series` (`null` for an appointment that happens once); `Updated` gives `added`: the occurrence changed apart, or the series that goes on.": "",
  "Now also `scope` and `series`.": "",
  "Now also `saved` and `unsaved` (each `{ kind, appointment, changes? }`) and `undone`: what a change of a series wrote before it failed, and whether it was all taken back.": "",
  "RecurrenceEditor": "",
  "The rule as RFC 5545 text; empty when it does not repeat. Two-way with `x-model`.": "",
